#### All of these are:
* #### Generative AI tools
* #### Built using Large Language Models
* #### Accessed through an AI chatbot interface

#### Most consumer AI tools, including all of the above, are now **multimodal**, meaning they can work with more than just text. They can understand and create content using text, images, audio, and sometimes video.

#### Users interact with these tools using prompts, usually through a AI chat interface.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Prompt Engineering:</strong> A technique that involves refining and adjusting the inputs given to AI models to achieve more accurate or desired outputs.</p>
</div>

#### There are a number of ways to format prompts to get better outputs from LLMs. One simple prompt engineering structure you can use is **TaCo FoRT**.

<p align="center">
<img src="https://images.code.org/a9b6ae8f94bfa64afbf2af4a60ec6609-Screenshot 2025-04-07 at 2.01.43 PM.png" alt="lesson plan diagram" width="70%" style="border-radius:10px; border: 5px solid black;">
</p>

#### Click **Continue** to learn more about the **TaCo FoRT** prompt structure.


